verdict.reason:
The 'Task ID / Worktree / Block reason' text is the user prompt built in orchestrator/src/orchestrator/dry_run_unblock.py. It reads 'Task ID: {task_id}
Worktree: {worktree}
Block reason: {reason}
Detail: ...

{task_context}

Investigate and emit your structured proposal.' scripts/legibility/reingestion.py::is_harness_injected_turn does not recognise it. Its briefing heading rule, HARNESS_HEADING_SETS, HARNESS_PROMPT_MARKERS and the '# context' memory-block rule all miss it. The only place that knows this shape is scripts/legibility/detectors.py::AGENT_CLASS_MARKERS, which uses it to classify the agent class, not to exclude the turn. As a result the digest bucket records the turn as a human 'User Correction'. This repeats the already-known harness-injected-prompt-as-User-Correction defect for one more injector shape. The 'mislabel as a task-failure bucket' framing is a symptom: the failure text is the harness's own prompt, not a user turn.

